                <pb facs="0613" n="603" sameAs="frus:frus1943China/pg603"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.24/1589: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in China</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Atcheson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-06-04T13:00:00-04:00">June 4, 1943—1
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>715. Department’s 651 of May 22, 9 p.m. Department understands British have
                    agreed to supply 550 trucks from stock in India and to man them.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
